bip340 — provenance note
=========================

Kept as a module-local NOTICE (same placement as the sibling `tlsresume`/
`dtls`/`falcon`/`slhdsa` modules, which are likewise self-contained crypto
modules not folded into the root `NOTICE`).

Provenance
----------

bip340 — clean-room implementation from BIP340 ("Schnorr Signatures for
secp256k1", bitcoin/bips), covering: the tagged-hash construction
("Design"), the x-only public key convention and `lift_x` ("Public Key
Conversion"), the default signing algorithm ("Default Signing"), the
verification algorithm ("Verification"), and batch verification ("Batch
Verification"). BIP340 is a public, open Bitcoin Improvement Proposal —
not a copyrightable work (merger doctrine; see CONVENTIONS.md §5) — so no
third-party-source NOTICE entry is strictly required for the spec citation
alone. No reference implementation's source was ported or consulted as a
design reference — neither for the scaffold nor for the crypto pass that
implemented the cores (`sign`/`verify`/`verifyBatch`): that pass worked
from the BIP340 specification text and the public API of
`std.crypto.ecc.Secp256k1` only (no `bitcoin-core/secp256k1` or other
implementation consulted).

The official BIP340 test vectors (`kat_vectors.zig`) were fetched directly
from `bip-0340/test-vectors.csv` in the `bitcoin/bips` repository
(https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bitcoin/bips/master/bip-0340/test-vectors.csv)
for this pass. This is a public specification artifact — the BIP's own
published conformance vectors — not copied from any other implementation's
test suite.

`std.crypto.ecc.Secp256k1` (field arithmetic, scalar arithmetic, point
group law, `basePoint`, `mul`/`mulDoubleBasePublic`, `recoverY`) and
`std.crypto.hash.sha2.Sha256` are used via their public APIs (MIT, part of
Zig itself); see `root.zig`'s and `hash.zig`'s module docs for the specific
recon findings (`recoverY` == BIP340's `lift_x`; `mulDoubleBasePublic` ==
the verify equation's `s*G + (-e mod n)*P`).

No GPL/LGPL/AGPL source was consulted or copied anywhere in this module.

